---
/*
  About "Our story", from Figma Section / Our story (93:1521).
  Copy as in Figma. Figma note: the edits to this text are waiting for
  client approval.
*/
import FramedPhoto from '../FramedPhoto.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../SectionHeading.astro';
import hug from '../../assets/photos/stock-health-workers-hug.jpg';
import smiling from '../../assets/photos/stock-health-worker-smiling.jpg';
---

<section class="section story" aria-labelledby="story-title" data-reveal>
  <div class="story__split">
    <FramedPhoto
      main={{ src: hug, alt: 'Four health workers in white coats hugging and smiling', fade: 'top' }}
      inset={{ src: smiling, alt: 'A smiling health worker holding the hands of a woman' }}
      desktopHeight="var(--size-story-photo-desktop)"
    />
    <div class="story__text">
      <SectionHeading id="story-title" eyebrow="Our Story" title="How OMWI began" />
      <p class="t-body">
        Born out of the strong belief that all women, regardless of where they come from, deserve
        safe and quality healthcare, Ọmụgwọ Maternal Welfare Initiative (OMWI) was created to stand
        in the gap between women in underserved communities and the care they need.
      </p>
      <p class="t-body">
        OMWI saw a gap in Nigeria’s women’s health landscape. Period poverty is widespread, and the
        country’s maternal mortality ratio is among the highest in the world. Leading causes of
        maternal illness and death in Nigeria include infection, postpartum haemorrhage and
        hypertensive disorders, which are largely preventable or treatable. With the right resources
        and advocacy, OMWI works to combat these causes and help bring maternal deaths down.
      </p>
      <p class="t-body">
        The spirit of ọmụgwọ is at the heart of our mission. Ọmụgwọ is a traditional practice of the
        Igbo people in which a new mother is herself mothered in the early weeks after birth by her
        own mother or another woman in her family. Respecting this traditional knowledge and care,
        OMWI extends the essence of ọmụgwọ through empowering health education and by facilitating
        access to quality healthcare.
      </p>
      <p class="t-body">
        Ultimately, with dedication to our vision we strive to achieve health and wellness for all
        women without borders.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .story__split {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--layout-split-gap);
  }
  .story__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-20);
  }
  .story__text p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  @media (min-width: 1200px) {
    .story__split {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
    .story__split > :global(*) {
      flex: 1 1 0;
      min-width: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
